            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> please trim AI reports before creating them. there's a lot of noise in this one.\n\nThis was after trimmed it to a third of the size 😆.\nI guess I didn't have the patience to trim it down further. I should probably just wrote it from scratch mysefl.\nSorry for pushing the burden on you.\n\n> so, don't do that? just schedule it via vim.schedule().\n\nI was actually trying to fix an issue in snacks (which I later found out it was https://github.com/folke/snacks.nvim/issues/2507), and warping it in `vim.schedule` seems like a bigger refactor then I would like.\n\n> fnamemodify() is supported from fast-contexts where possible, but we don't promise to support e.g. features that require Vimscript (:s modifiers).\n\nWould you suggest that I use a more \"lua native\" api, like `vim.fs.abspath` instead?\nMy worry about it is that I saw in [here](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/4a0859631407bc9279a935f3219faabc0991a826/runtime/lua/vim/fs.lua#L869) that you intend to change it to use `vim.f.fnamemodify`.",
