            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> This was after trimmed it to a third of the size 😆.\n\nno worries, it's actually not that bad :)\n\n\n\n>  `vim.fs.abspath` ... My worry about it is that I saw in [here](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/4a0859631407bc9279a935f3219faabc0991a826/runtime/lua/vim/fs.lua#L869) that you intend to change it to use `vim.f.fnamemodify`.\n\nyeah exactly.\n\nideally, we should find a way to make more `fnamemodify()` features work without tripping the \"not so fast\" alarm.\n\nresolving `~user` seems like something we can support without tripping that. probably env vars too, if we don't already.\n\nthe only thing we probably can't support is `:s`, but that's pretty esoteric anyway.",
