            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "do you think we really need the fallback in `expand_env_esc`? https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/4a0859631407bc9279a935f3219faabc0991a826/src/nvim/os/env.c#L648-L661\n\nIt seems to me that what we do before - isolating the username and calling `getpwnam` - is what the expected behavior on unix systems.\n\nI took a quick look in [bash](https://github.com/gitGNU/gnu_bash/blob/master/lib/tilde/tilde.c#L343) and [fish](https://github.com/fish-shell/fish-shell/blob/c5042d99885b790acacc9836fff1a6c47c30531a/src/expand.rs#L1107)'s source code and they seem to be doing the same thing.\n\nCould we just remove the fallback to the shell to solve this?\nI can open a PR if you think this is a good idea :)",
